From ba6f0123b20c71c56fcd59730850ebce2da7c419 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roger Hernando <rogerhb@meta.com>
Date: Tue, 9 Jun 2026 18:25:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 63/63] [cuttlefish][darwin-host-tools] Backport
 --extra_qemu_args passthrough

Summary:
The darwin-aarch64 cuttlefish host tools shipped with device drops are built
from <internal-branch>, which is
substantially behind the upstream cuttlefish that carries the
--extra_qemu_args flag. On this branch the flag is MISSING entirely:
launch_cvd -extra_qemu_args=... fails with "unknown command line flag
'extra_qemu_args'", so QEMU+Crashpad config cannot be forwarded through
Cuttlefish on macOS.

This ports the full feature (not just D106842176's comma-truncation fix,
since there is nothing here to fix yet), plumbed through every layer and
modeled on the existing qemu_binary_dir flag and the extra_bootconfig_args
per-instance vector config:

- assemble_cvd/flags_defaults.h: add CF_DEFAULTS_EXTRA_QEMU_ARGS ("").
- assemble_cvd/flags.cc: DEFINE_string(extra_qemu_args, ...); in the
  per-instance loop, read FLAGS_extra_qemu_args DIRECTLY (not via
  GET_FLAG_STR_VALUE(), whose helper splits on ',' -- cuttlefish's
  per-instance separator -- which would truncate qemu args that legitimately
  contain commas). This carries forward D106842176's key insight so
  comma-containing crashpad args survive intact.
- cuttlefish_config.{h,cpp}: add InstanceSpecific extra_qemu_args() getter and
  set_extra_qemu_args() setter. Stored as a raw string, space-split on read
  (mirrors extra_bootconfig_args).
- vm_manager/qemu_manager.cpp: forward each arg to the QEMU command via
  AddParameter just before the command is finalized.

Net effect matches the live Linux behavior: a single comma-joined
-extra_qemu_args="-crashpad enable=on,database=...,url=...,annotation=..."
reaches qemu without truncation.

Test Plan:
E2e tets by compiling host tools, patching and running via device:

Sync mac host repo:
```
mkdir -p ~/cvd-tools && cd ~/cvd-tools
repo init -u ssh://git-ro.vip.facebook.com/data/gitrepos/aosp/manifest.git \
  --repo-url=ssh://git.vip.facebook.com/data/gitrepos/osmeta/external/repo.git \
  --repo-branch=master \
  --current-branch --no-repo-verify --no-tags -b <internal-branch> \
  --no-clone-bundle
repo sync -c -d --no-tags --force-sync -j12
```
Do changes and build teh host tools:
```
source build/envsetup.sh && lunch aosp_cf_arm64_phone-userdebug
m out/host/darwin-x86/cvd-host_package.tar.gz
```

Patched host tools into the device cache.. --skip-build-hash-check
stops device from re-validating and clobbering the patched binaries.
```
device=~/.device/cache/emulators/<device>_cf_emu_arm64-83500000003761-2029679934606809
cp out/host/darwin-x86/bin/{assemble_cvd,run_cvd} "$device/bin/"
rm -rf "$device/cuttlefish"   # force fresh assembly
mkdir -p ~/cvd-e2e/crashpad-db-bundled

device device emulator -t device --skip-build-hash-check \
  --extra-emu-args='-extra_qemu_args="-crashpad enable=on,database=/Users/rogerhb/cvd-e2e/crashpad-db-bundled,url=https://developer.147447.od.oculus.com/emulator/crash/,handler='"$device"'/qemu-cf/darwin-aarch64/libexec/crashpad_handler,annotation=maui_command_id:rogerhb-T275117255-e2e"'
```

Check the QEMU cmdline to validate options are passed correctly:
```
QPID=$(pgrep -f "qemu-system-aarch64 -name guest=cvd-1" | head -1)
ps -o command= -p "$QPID" | grep -o '\-crashpad enable=on[^ ]*'
# -crashpad enable=on,database=/Users/rogerhb/cvd-e2e/crashpad-db-bundled,url=https://developer.147447.od.oculus.com/emulator/crash/,handler=<cache>/qemu-cf/darwin-aarch64/libexec/crashpad_handler,annotation=maui_command_id:rogerhb-T275117255-e2e
```

Trigger a crash and confirm the OD breakpoint catches it:
```
kill -SEGV "$QPID"
ls ~/cvd-e2e/crashpad-db-bundled/pending/     # dedce754-...dmp  (HELD)
ls ~/cvd-e2e/crashpad-db-bundled/completed/    # empty - held at breakpoint
```
Validate crash hits OD breakpoint on developer.147447.od.oculus.com HIT, carrying
annotation maui_command_id:rogerhb-T275117255-e2e.
{F1991028076}

Once breakpoint is released crash report flips to completed
```
ls ~/cvd-e2e/crashpad-db-bundled/completed/
dedce754-9b01-47e5-9cba-4c3353d8b313.dmp
```

